# Context boundaries

When working a contribution-runway ticket, Treat `allowed_read_paths` as the context boundary and
`allowed_write_paths` as the edit boundary.

Do not infer that permission to read a file grants permission to modify it.

## Restricted areas

The following remain blocked even when named as the ticket `area`:

- `packages/core/**`
- `packages/nodes-base/credentials/**`
- Identity and access-management code
- Team-owned high-impact nodes listed in policy

Proceed only when the deterministic checker confirms a separate owner approval
record containing an approver and approval reference.

The ticket must not authorize its own exception.

## Rules of engagement

- Do not open or modify files outside the allowed context to "make the fix easier."
- Do not broaden a bug fix into a cross-cutting refactor.
- If the needed fix clearly lives outside the allowed directory, stop and report that the ticket area/policy must change — do not expand scope yourself.
- Keep `maximum_scope` from policy in mind; prefer a small, focused change.
